userStories.description:
**Goal** — Provide a never-throwing read-only live PR status reader sharing existing thread and writer policy.

**Motivation** — `workflowStatusCommand` (`packages/nax/src/cli/workflow.ts`) reads only the run's `result.json`, written at publish time; rulings live on the PR.

**Approach** — Add `workflow/live-status.ts` with `readLiveStatus`, export `canRule` from `workflow/promote-rulings.ts`, and reuse `readPrState`, `readItemThreads` and `settleItemThreads`.

An item is matched to its thread by `ItemThread.itemId` (the id parsed from the thread opener) for threads in the PR's `w-index`; no `itemKey` hash comparison is done, so a run-record item whose `kind` or `issue` differs from the published opener still matches by id. The `items` input limits the returned ids to those present in the run record. A PR with no `w-index` comment returns `{ source: "run-record", error: "no nax item index on this PR" }`. It never throws and never writes to the forge. `canRule` in `promote-rulings.ts` is exported so both readers share one writer check.

`readPromoteRulings` in `packages/nax/src/workflow/promote-rulings.ts` already performs the read-only PR read this feature needs for status: `prNumberFromUrl`, `resolvePrRef`, `readCurrentUser`, `listReviewThreads`, `listPrComments`, then `readItemThreads` and `settleItemThreads` with a `hasWriteAccess`-backed `canRule`. `readPrState(forge, prRef, deps, cwd)` in `packages/nax/src/workflow/pr-state.ts` returns `{ isDraft, body, url? }` and throws `WORKFLOW_PR_READ_FAILED`.

Partition the shared settled items: a confirmed advisor with no fixClosed goes into awaitingFix, not settled; a fix-closed one goes into settled with disposition confirmed. A kept writer reply reopens either through the existing reply rules.

Failure handling: The run record's url carries no PR number (`prNumberFromUrl` returns null): no live read is attempted and no forge command runs; `nax workflow status` reports the run record with `source` `run-record` and no `liveError`. `readLiveStatus` cannot detect a forge, or any forge read throws: it returns `{ source: "run-record", error }`, and `nax workflow status` reports the run record and `liveError`. At this reader boundary, a URL without a PR number returns the run-record error union before any forge invocation; the CLI's no-liveError eligibility guard belongs to US-007. Forge-state read failures that propagate to readLiveStatus produce the error union. Permission lookup exceptions already caught by the shared canRule remain denied replies, preserving that helper's existing fail-closed behavior rather than converting them into fatal status-read errors. The no-write test must assert both a live result for successful read fixtures and an empty mutation-call list: catching a fake write exception into run-record fallback would not prove read-only behavior.

**Scope** — In: new reader, exported shared canRule, read-only PR state/index/ownership/permission settlement, id matching, and fake-forge tests. Out: CLI report formatting/eligibility (US-007), bot recorder/review/fix changes (US-002 through US-005), and changing local workflow promote/record confirmation semantics.

**Interface** — Verbatim new module contract:
```ts
export type LiveStatus =
  | {
      readonly source: "live";
      readonly isDraft: boolean;
      /** Item ids whose thread carries a ruling that closes the item. */
      readonly settled: readonly { readonly id: string; readonly disposition: string }[];
      /** Item ids that are confirmed advisor items with no fix-closing reply. */
      readonly awaitingFix: readonly string[];
    }
  | { readonly source: "run-record"; readonly error: string };

export function readLiveStatus(input: {
  readonly url: string;
  readonly cwd: string;
  readonly deps: ForgeDeps;
  readonly items: readonly OpenItem[];
}): Promise<LiveStatus>;
```
